 <div class="fit-pitch" id="presentation"><p class="label">MY INTRODUCTION / ABOUT 90 SECONDS</p><h3>“My strength is connecting policy, data and execution.”</h3><p>In enterprise AI governance, I have worked on the practical questions behind adoption: what information a reviewer needs, where decisions become ambiguous, and how to make guidance useful. I analyzed more than 800 approval requests and delivered interactive reports that made classification gaps and unresolved workflow issues visible.</p><p>I also processed more than 2,000 multilingual automation cases in Python, refined categories and built dashboards with clear units of analysis. In human–AI research, I contributed to evaluation work involving more than 10 model candidates and 30 experimental conditions, investigating whether inconsistent behavior came from prompts, information states or the rules themselves.</p><p>That is the foundation I would bring to Handshake: clear review workflows, careful analysis and decision-ready communication. I would apply it to policy rubrics, reviewer calibration and quality reporting. My direct experience is in enterprise governance and research; I would learn the project’s safety policies and sensitive-content procedures before taking on independent judgments. I want to help teams understand why decisions differ, improve the guidance and measure whether the next batch is better.</p></div>
